1. git fetch origin. Check whether __STAGING__ is ahead of __INTEGRATION__:
   git rev-list --count origin/__INTEGRATION__..origin/__STAGING__
   If 0, say "conductor: __INTEGRATION__ up to date" and wait for the next cycle.

2. Use a DETACHED checkout of __STAGING__'s remote-tracking ref, not the local __STAGING__ branch (issue #91: git only lets ONE worktree hold a given branch at a time, so if any other worktree — an implementer mid-claim, a QA self-check — has the local __STAGING__ branch checked out, `git switch __STAGING__` here fails and stalls every promotion until it clears; detaching means this step can NEVER be locked out by another worktree):
